+// cranvr: whether data that arrived at `arrival` is no older than `limit` at `now`. A reader reads the clock
+// before it waits for the lock, and the receiver sets `arrival` under that lock. A message that the receiver
+// handled while the reader waited has an arrival after the reader's `now`: that is the newest data, not
+// stale data. Counting it as stale made a hand's pose flicker between valid and invalid under load, mostly the
+// hand of the last pose message of a sample (the right one).
+bool arrivedWithin(XrTime arrival, XrTime now, XrDuration limit) {
+    return arrival > 0 && (now < arrival || now - arrival <= limit);
+}
